1. Permitted use

Under these terms, you may download an authorized official copy
free of charge, install and run it, and make a reasonable backup for
your own use. Personal, educational, research, and commercial use are
permitted, including using Vespera in a business and building and
monetizing your own independent AI projects. The permission is
nonexclusive, nontransferable, and subject to these terms.

2. Ownership and user work

Vespera's proprietary code, documentation, and branding remain the
property of their respective rights holders. Use of Vespera does not
transfer ownership in either direction. You retain any rights you have
in your data, prompts, workflows, outputs, and independently created
work. Rights in third-party inputs, models, and outputs remain subject
to applicable law and their own terms.

3. Restrictions

Except with the relevant rights holder's separate written permission or
as permitted by applicable law or a component's own license, you may not
modify Vespera, create derivative versions of it, distribute or
redistribute it or a derivative version, resell it, sublicense it, or
repackage it. These restrictions apply to Vespera itself. No open-source
license to Vespera or right to publish modified builds is granted. This
license grants no right to imply endorsement or use Vespera branding as
your own.

4. Interoperability

You may develop, distribute, and monetize independent integrations that
use supported interfaces without incorporating proprietary Vespera
material. Nothing in this license restricts non-waivable rights,
including applicable rights to study, test, or obtain information needed
for interoperability.

5. Third-party components

Third-party software, fonts, and assets retain their own terms. This
license does not supersede those terms or limit permissions they grant.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the applicable upstream notices.
Separately obtained services, models, and model weights have their own
